XDJ-RX patch 15: sub-ucom LED back-channel (rbp -> panel MCU SubTxData).

The MOSI half of every sub-ucom SPI burst is rbp's SubTxData: LED, level-meter
and jog-ring state for the panel MCU. Capture it, un-swap it (same per-32-bit-word
byte reversal as MISO), gate on its CRC-16/X-25 (20-byte payload, CRC LE at 0x16),
and publish each change as one text line "T <40 hex>\n":
  - socket mode: back up the xdjctrl chardev (the panel server's connection),
    non-blocking; re-sent to a newly connected client;
  - file mode:   XDJ_TX_PATH (default /tmp/subucom_tx), atomically replaced.
XDJ_TX_LOG=1 logs every changed burst to stderr (RE aid).
Byte/bit layout: docs/subucom-led-map.md.

